JSB-Betay Development Organization BDO 1- 300 members are selected to clean Tokar city in the activity of cash for work. 2- BDO is in the process of making a fish market by starting to make shelter and tables. 3- Betay have challenges of accessing their money by transferring it from Mashrag bank to bank of khartoum this cause delay in achieving activities 4- The misunderstanding of the boutique women group is not solved yet it becomes the general opinion and city talk there is likely or probability of fraud smell. {your advice is needed}
JSB: JVC: • Construction of a community building in the Hushairi area to benefit the local population. • Procurement of 32 goats, each accompanied by its kid, to ensure high milk production. • The goats were vaccinated by a veterinary doctor. • Training of community committee members on leadership skills.15 men • Coordination for training fishermen to equip them with skills that enhance their efficiency and productivity targeting 60 .
CM-Update: (1) 7 male and 3 female (the representative of ministry of agriculture at locality level) received training on vegetables production, post harvesting operation and climate change. They come across such topics like the impact of climate change on natural resources and mitigation measures and others. (2) Today marks the 13th day of the Environmental Sanitation Campaign. The team will complete their work next week, on Saturday and Sunday. (3) At the beginning of the week, the Minister of Human Resources and Social Development, accompanied by the Governor of the Red Sea State, visited the organization, reviewed its activities, praised the Environmental Sanitation Campaign, and confirmed their full readiness to cooperate and facilitate any challenges facing the organization. (4) Yesterday, there was also a visit by Sovereign Council member Dr. Nawara Bafli, along with the Governor of the Red Sea State and a number of security, police, military, executive, and community leaders. They witnessed the large number of young men and women from the area actively participating in the Environmental Sanitation Campaign. They commended the organization, its projects, and its significant role in serving and developing the people of the Sinkatlocality.
